bral and costotransverse joint pain: A commonly overlooked pain generator</article-title><source>Top Clin Chiro</source><year>1999</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>79</fpage><lpage>92</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>DeFranca</surname><given-names>GG</given-names></name><name><surname>Levine</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The T4 syndrome</article-title><source>J Manipulative Physiol Ther</source><year>1995</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>34</fpage><lpage>37</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7706958</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flynn</surname><given-names>TW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Thoracic spine and ribcage disorders</article-title><source>Orthopaedic Physical Therapy Clinics of North America</source><year>1999</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>20</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McGuckin</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><source>The T4 Syndrome</source><year>1986</year><publisher-name>London: Churchill Livingstone</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ezekiel</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Persellin</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Costovertebral and costotransverse joint involvement in rheumatoid arthritis</article-title><source>Ann Rheum Dis</source><year>1978</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>473</fpage><lpage>475</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">718281</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/ard.37.5.473</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><